        "text": "What's the most you would spend on pizza? In 2010, a hungry Bitcoin enthusiast decided to try something unique. Could he order real world pizzas with the new digital currency on a forum? He offered 10,000 bitcoin in exchange for someone ordering two large pizzas to his house. The offer was accepted, the bitcoin transferred and the pizzas delivered. Boom. The first bitcoin transaction was written into legend. The only kicker, the 10,000 Bitcoin used to pay for the pizzas are literally, literally worth hundreds of millions of dollars today. So next time you think of buying pizza with crypto, take a moment to consider if they are really that tasty.",
